# Change @host to https://localhost:7047 if you're running `dotnet run` directly.
@host = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json
@serial = R2R-{{$timestamp}}

### 1) Create a fresh product (unique serial via {{$timestamp}})
POST {{host}}/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Right-to-Repair Blender",
  "brand": "KitchenCo",
  "serial": "{{serial}}",
  "purchaseDate": "2024-03-01",
  "warrantyMonths": 24,
  "retailer": "Example Store",
  "price": 249.50
}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); %}
> {% client.global.set("productSerial", response.body.serial); %}

### 2) Query products by the exact serial we just saved
GET {{host}}/products?q={{productSerial}}

### 3) Fetch warranty status (should be in warranty right after purchase)
GET {{host}}/products/{{productId}}/in-warranty

### 4) Check expiring products (45 day window snapshot)
GET {{host}}/products/expiring?days=45

### 5) Open a repair with Right-to-Repair consent
POST {{host}}/repairs
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "productId": {{productId}},
  "openedAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "notes": "Motor stalls when blending frozen fruit",
  "consumerOptedForRepair": true
}

> {% client.global.set("repairId", response.body.id); %}

### 6) List open repairs (new case should appear here)
GET {{host}}/repairs?status=Open

### 7) Advance repair to InProgress
PATCH {{host}}/repairs/{{repairId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "InProgress"
}

### 8) Complete the repair (mark as Fixed to trigger the warranty extension)
PATCH {{host}}/repairs/{{repairId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "Fixed"
}

### 9) Fetch summary report (counts & averages now include this repair)
GET {{host}}/reports/summary

### 10) Re-check warranty status (fixed repairs with consent earn an extra 12 months)
GET {{host}}/products/{{productId}}/in-warranty

### 11) Clean up: delete the demo product (cascades repairs for repeatable runs)
DELETE {{host}}/products/{{productId}}

### 12) Confirm the product no longer exists under that serial
GET {{host}}/products?q={{productSerial}}
